a NATO military leader is raising new  concerns this morning about Russia's  massive military exercise underway in  Eastern Europe  the head of NATO's Military Committee  says the war games could be a serious  suit could be as seen serious a surge  preparation for a big war despite  Russian assurances they pose no threat  the week-long exercise has taken place  in areas near the Baltic Sea involves  thousands of personnel tanks and  aircraft Elizabeth Palmer is near Saint  Petersburg Russia she's on the ground  with Russian troops good morning these  exercises are certainly a real workout  for the various branches of the Russian  Armed Forces but they're also intended  as spectacle with the pictures of the  action intended for broadcast around the  world the message especially to the US  and its NATO allies is taking on Russia  would be a mistake NATO is watching  carefully it says as many as a hundred  thousand Russian and Belarusian troops  are taking part  the Russians say that's nonsense there  are only just under 13,000 the truth  lies probably somewhere in the middle  but the lack of transparency adds to the  threatening tone Russia stages huge  military exercises every four years but  this one is exceptional because part of  it is taking place in neighboring  Belarus to the west which puts those  thousands of troops  nose-to-nose against NATO forces just  across the border for CBS this morning  I'm Elizabeth Palmer in luga south of  st. Petersburg
 

